[{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000001","text":"Cats can rotate each ear independently and direct it toward a sound without moving their head. This ability helps them pinpoint quiet rustling and other subtle noises with impressive accuracy.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":128},"createdAt":"2022-06-29T09:15:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000002","text":"A group of adult cats is commonly called a clowder, while a group of kittens may be called a kindle. These traditional terms are uncommon in everyday conversation but remain part of English vocabulary.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":94},"createdAt":"2022-06-18T14:30:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000003","text":"A cat uses its whiskers to detect tiny changes in nearby air currents and sense objects that are difficult to see. Whiskers also help the animal estimate whether its body can pass through a narrow opening.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":176},"createdAt":"2022-06-04T08:05:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000004","text":"Most domestic cats sleep for roughly twelve to sixteen hours during a typical day, although the exact amount varies. Their sleep is divided into many short periods, with both light dozing and deeper rest.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":51},"createdAt":"2022-05-22T18:45:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000005","text":"Powerful muscles in the hind legs allow a healthy cat to jump several times its own height. Before leaping, the cat often shifts its weight and carefully measures the distance to the landing point.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":203},"createdAt":"2022-05-09T11:20:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000006","text":"The rough surface of a cat tongue is covered with tiny backward-facing structures called papillae. They act like a built-in comb, helping remove loose fur and spread natural oils through the coat.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":87},"createdAt":"2022-04-27T16:10:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000007","text":"Cats communicate through a combination of vocal sounds, facial expressions, tail positions, and body posture. A meow intended for a person can carry a very different meaning from a hiss or a relaxed purr.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":42},"createdAt":"2022-04-12T07:55:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000008","text":"Cats possess an additional scent-detecting structure called the vomeronasal organ in the roof of the mouth. When investigating an interesting smell, a cat may briefly open its mouth to draw scent molecules toward this organ.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":119},"createdAt":"2022-04-02T12:00:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000009","text":"A cat tail supports balance when the animal walks along a narrow surface or changes direction quickly. Its position and movement also communicate emotions such as confidence, uncertainty, irritation, or fear.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":156},"createdAt":"2022-03-31T10:25:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000000a","text":"Kittens are born with their eyes closed because their visual system is still developing. The eyes usually begin opening after about one week, and clear vision continues to improve during the following weeks.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":33},"createdAt":"2022-03-15T19:05:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000000b","text":"Cats can hear sounds at frequencies much higher than the upper limit of human hearing. This sensitivity is especially useful for detecting the high-pitched noises made by small prey.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":221},"createdAt":"2022-02-20T06:50:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000000c","text":"A slow blink is often displayed by a relaxed cat that feels safe in its surroundings. People can gently return the gesture, although the rest of the animal body language should always be considered as well.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":73},"createdAt":"2022-01-08T15:35:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000000d","text":"Cats use scent to exchange information about territory, familiarity, and social relationships. They may rub their cheeks against furniture or people to leave scent from glands around the face.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":28},"createdAt":"2021-12-17T12:00:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000000e","text":"The highly flexible spine of a cat contributes to its speed, agility, and long running stride. Flexibility also helps the animal twist its body while falling and prepare its feet for landing.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":144},"createdAt":"2021-11-03T17:25:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000000f","text":"When walking, cats commonly move the front and rear legs on one side before moving the legs on the other side. This unusual gait helps produce the smooth and controlled motion associated with feline movement.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":98},"createdAt":"2021-09-14T09:45:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000010","text":"A healthy adult cat normally has thirty permanent teeth adapted for gripping, cutting, and tearing food. Regular dental care matters because cats can develop painful gum and tooth disease without obvious early symptoms.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":19},"createdAt":"2021-07-02T14:15:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000011","text":"Cats groom their fur to remove dirt and loose hair while distributing protective natural oils. Evaporation of saliva left on the coat can also contribute to cooling when the surrounding temperature rises.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":167},"createdAt":"2021-05-26T08:30:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000012","text":"The domestic cat belongs to the species Felis catus and shares many behaviors with its wild relatives. Even a well-fed house cat may stalk toys, hide before pouncing, and patrol familiar territory.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":112},"createdAt":"2021-03-19T20:10:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000013","text":"Most cats have five toes on each front paw and four toes on each rear paw. Some inherit a trait called polydactyly, which gives them additional toes on one or more feet.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":37},"createdAt":"2021-01-12T11:55:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000014","text":"The surface of every cat nose has a distinctive arrangement of small ridges and grooves. Like many other biological patterns, the detailed texture varies from one individual animal to another.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":189},"createdAt":"2020-11-04T07:20:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000015","text":"Cats see particularly well in dim light because their eyes are adapted to collect more available light than human eyes. They still require some light to see and cannot navigate in complete darkness using vision alone.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":134},"createdAt":"2022-06-25T10:10:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000016","text":"A cat has a small, free-floating collarbone that is not rigidly attached to the other bones of the shoulder. This anatomy contributes to a flexible stride and helps the body move through tight spaces.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":61},"createdAt":"2022-06-14T13:20:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000017","text":"Most cats can extend their claws when climbing, hunting, stretching, or defending themselves and retract them while resting. Keeping the claws sheathed reduces wear and helps them remain sharp.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":148},"createdAt":"2022-06-01T08:40:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000018","text":"Cats may purr when they are comfortable, but purring can also occur during stress, pain, or uncertainty. The surrounding situation and the rest of the body language are needed to interpret the sound.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":76},"createdAt":"2022-05-28T17:05:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000019","text":"Scent glands around the face, paws, and other parts of the body help cats mark familiar objects and locations. Scent marking creates an invisible layer of information that other cats can investigate.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":182},"createdAt":"2022-05-19T09:50:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000001a","text":"A cat sense of smell is far more sensitive than that of a human and plays a major role in daily life. Smell helps cats assess food, identify familiar individuals, and investigate changes in their environment.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":49},"createdAt":"2022-05-11T15:30:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000001b","text":"Cats have a protective third eyelid called the nictitating membrane near the inner corner of each eye. It can help protect and moisten the eye, but persistent visibility may indicate that veterinary attention is needed.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":117},"createdAt":"2022-05-03T07:25:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000001c","text":"Cats are digitigrade animals, which means they normally walk on their toes rather than placing the entire foot on the ground. This posture lengthens the functional limb and supports quiet, agile movement.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":65},"createdAt":"2022-04-25T18:15:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000001d","text":"Feline hunting behavior often follows a sequence that includes watching, stalking, chasing, pouncing, and grabbing. Indoor play that imitates this sequence can give a cat an appropriate outlet for natural behavior.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":159},"createdAt":"2022-04-18T11:45:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000001e","text":"A cat pupil can narrow to a vertical slit in bright conditions and expand dramatically when light is scarce. Pupil size also changes with arousal, so it should not be interpreted without considering the environment.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":82},"createdAt":"2022-04-11T16:35:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000001f","text":"Domestic cats evolved from desert-adapted ancestors and often obtain a meaningful portion of their water from food. Cats eating dry diets still need constant access to clean, appealing drinking water.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":126},"createdAt":"2022-04-06T06:55:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000020","text":"Kneading is the rhythmic motion in which a cat presses its front paws alternately against a soft surface. The behavior begins during nursing and may continue into adulthood when the cat feels relaxed or secure.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":58},"createdAt":"2022-04-03T12:30:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000021","text":"Many adult cats have reduced ability to digest lactose, so ordinary cow milk can cause digestive upset. Fresh water and nutritionally complete cat food are safer routine choices than a bowl of milk.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":143},"createdAt":"2022-03-29T10:05:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000022","text":"Loose fur swallowed during grooming can collect in the stomach and occasionally be expelled as a hairball. Frequent vomiting, appetite changes, or difficulty passing stool should be discussed with a veterinarian.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":71},"createdAt":"2022-03-10T14:45:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000023","text":"Cats often build predictable routines around feeding, resting, play, and interaction with people. Sudden changes to those routines can be stressful, especially when the animal has little control over its surroundings.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":196},"createdAt":"2022-02-26T08:20:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000024","text":"The feline righting reflex helps a falling cat rotate its body and orient its feet toward the ground. It does not guarantee a safe landing, and falls from windows or balconies can cause severe injuries.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":54},"createdAt":"2022-02-03T19:10:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000025","text":"Play allows kittens to practice movements used in hunting, communication, and social interaction. Adult cats also benefit from regular play that matches their age, mobility, confidence, and individual preferences.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":165},"createdAt":"2022-01-21T09:35:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000026","text":"Positive experiences with people, animals, sounds, and handling during kittenhood can influence later behavior. Introductions should remain gentle and controlled because overwhelming exposure can create fear instead of confidence.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":46},"createdAt":"2021-12-29T13:55:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000027","text":"A cat tail contains a series of small vertebrae surrounded by muscles, nerves, and connective tissue. Tail injuries can be serious because nerves in the area may also affect movement and other body functions.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":137},"createdAt":"2021-11-18T07:40:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000028","text":"The shoulder blades of a cat are attached to the body mainly by muscles rather than by a rigid bony joint. This arrangement gives the front of the body a wide range of motion during running and climbing.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":68},"createdAt":"2021-10-07T16:25:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000029","text":"Cats have sweat glands in their paw pads, although sweating is not their main method of cooling. Damp paw prints can sometimes appear when a cat is hot, frightened, or experiencing significant stress.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":174},"createdAt":"2021-08-23T11:15:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000002a","text":"Cats lack a fully functional taste receptor for sweetness and do not perceive sweet flavors the way humans do. Their taste system is specialized for the dietary needs of an obligate carnivore.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":57},"createdAt":"2021-07-11T18:50:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000002b","text":"A reflective layer behind the retina called the tapetum lucidum sends light through the eye a second time. It improves vision in dim conditions and produces the familiar eye shine seen when light reaches feline eyes at night.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":188},"createdAt":"2021-06-02T06:30:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000002c","text":"Kittens first develop a set of temporary baby teeth and later replace them with permanent adult teeth. Teething can increase chewing behavior, but painful gums or retained teeth require professional assessment.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":63},"createdAt":"2021-04-16T12:40:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000002d","text":"Cats are often most active around dawn and dusk, a pattern described as crepuscular activity. A household schedule can influence this rhythm, and many cats adapt their active periods to regular feeding and play.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":151},"createdAt":"2021-03-05T15:05:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000002e","text":"Feline coat colors and patterns are produced by combinations of genes that control pigment type, distribution, and intensity. Environmental factors can affect coat condition, but the underlying pattern is largely inherited.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":44},"createdAt":"2021-01-24T09:25:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac0000000000000000002f","text":"Nearly all calico cats are female because the orange and black coat-color genes are carried on the X chromosome. Rare male calico cats can occur through unusual chromosome combinations or genetic events.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":207},"createdAt":"2020-11-13T17:35:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000030","text":"Research suggests that cats can distinguish familiar human voices and may learn the sounds used as their names. Recognizing a sound does not guarantee an obvious response, especially when the cat lacks motivation to react.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":79},"createdAt":"2020-09-28T08:15:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000031","text":"When a cat gently rubs its forehead or cheeks against a person, the behavior is often called bunting. It combines friendly social contact with scent marking from glands located around the face.","status":{"verified":true,"sentCount":163},"createdAt":"2020-07-09T14:20:00 +0000"},{"_id":"66ac00000000000000000032","text":"Scratching helps a cat maintain its claws, stretch its muscles, and leave both visual and scent marks. Providing stable scratching surfaces in preferred locations makes it easier to direct this normal behavior away from furniture.","status":{"verified":false,"sentCount":52},"createdAt":"2020-05-17T10:45:00 +0000"}]